# Web (`apps/web`)

One `QueryClient` (see `src/lib/query-client.ts` + `main.tsx`). Server state
goes through TanStack Query hooks. Local UI state is React state. No Redux.

Fetch **relative** `/api/...` only. The Vite+ proxy forwards to
`API_PROXY_TARGET`. Never call `localhost:3000` from the browser.

```ts
// ✅
const json: unknown = await (await fetch("/api/health")).json();
return healthResponseSchema.parse(json);

// ❌
const data = (await res.json()) as HealthResponse;
await fetch("http://localhost:3000/api/health");
```

The UI is the auth form, the health card (`useHealth`), the user's workspace
list (`useWorkspaces`) and the project board. `authClient`
(`src/lib/auth-client.ts`) is the only `createAuthClient()`, without `baseURL`
(same origin through the proxy). Form state is local React state, validated
with the shared sign-up/sign-in schemas. No React Router: `App.tsx` keeps
`selectedProjectId` as local state; the dashboard opens a project's board and
`BoardScreen` has a back button.

Board: `useBoard(projectId, userId)` (`boardQueryKey(projectId, userId)` →
`["board", projectId, userId]`) is the single source of the board; a 404 throws
`BoardNotFoundError` (no retry, "not found" state with a back button). Never
copy the board into `useState`; React state is only for the open dialog and
form text. `useTaskMutations(projectId, userId)` returns `createTask`,
`updateTask` and `deleteTask`; each `mutationKey` starts with
`boardMutationKey(projectId)` (`["board", projectId, …]`), which Session 3 uses
with `useIsMutating`. After each mutation update the cache and invalidate the
board query. Components in `src/components/`: `board-screen`, `kanban-board`,
`kanban-column`, `kanban-card` and `task-form-dialog` (one dialog, create and
edit modes).

Drag-and-drop uses `@dnd-kit/react` 0.5.1 only (`DragDropProvider`,
`useDroppable` in the column `<section>` with `collisionPriority: 1`,
`useSortable` from `@dnd-kit/react/sortable` in the card with
`group = column.id`); never `@dnd-kit/helpers`, `@dnd-kit/core` or
`@dnd-kit/sortable`, and do not import from `@dnd-kit/dom`. `onDragEnd` ignores
canceled operations; a drop on the free area of a column other than
`source.group` appends at its end; otherwise, if the optimistic sorting plugin
already moved the source (group or index changed), it persists
`source.group`/`source.index`; nothing changed → no API call. `useMoveTask(projectId,
userId)` (`mutationKey: ["board", projectId, "move"]`) is optimistic:
`onMutate` cancels the board query, snapshots it and applies the pure
`applyBoardMove` from `@agentic-kanban/schemas`; `onError` restores the
snapshot and calls `toast.error`; `onSettled` invalidates the board only
when it is the last board mutation in flight. A failed refetch with cached
data keeps the board on screen (full-screen error only without data). dnd-kit
reorders DOM nodes while dragging, so `KanbanBoard` remounts the provider with a
`key` derived from the board's order. Never keep a copy of the board in state.

Cache convention: every query of user data puts the `userId` in its queryKey
(`workspacesQueryKey(userId)` → `["workspaces", userId]`), and sign-out calls
`queryClient.clear()`, so switching users in one tab never shows the previous
user's data. `workspaceAccent(workspaceId)` (`src/lib/workspace-accent.ts`) is
pure and depends only on `workspace.id`, never on names or user data.

- App imports: `@/hooks/...`, `@/components/ui/...` with `.tsx` where the file
  uses that style. Generated shadcn under `src/components/ui` — do not restyle
  unless the task is UI.
- Compose classes with `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`.
- Tailwind 4 via `@import "tailwindcss"` in `src/index.css`. No `tailwind.config`.
- `next-themes` is the theme helper, not Next.js. Do not add Next, React Router,
  or React Hook Form.
- After `bunx shadcn@4.22.0 add …`, re-pin every new dependency (never `@latest`).
